  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><em>Category: Seen Gods</em></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">Primarily Practiced in: Zahnheim, North Rodda</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">Espirian Domains: The Heavens (Valtal, Khuldin)</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:bold\">The Disciplined represents the care, sacrifice, and commitment to a cause. People who worship this seat and its current occupant, Etronia, are commonly champions, soldiers, knights or healers, due to the edicts she espouses. Whether the cause is to someone else, to a greater deed, or oneself, Etronia encourages one to pour their blood, sweat and tears to the effort. Etronia appears as a garou loupain in loose robes wielding a hammer.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Title</strong> The Disciplined</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\">Edicts</strong> Commit yourself to your cause, sacrifice in the name of others</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\">Anathema</strong> Be selfish when your cause demands your all, put others in harm’s way</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Areas of Concern</strong> Commitment, healing, sacrifice</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Religious Symbol</strong> A heart upon a shield</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Animal</strong> Hermit Crab</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Colors</strong> blue and purple</span></p>"
